  "notes": [
    "[THIS PRODUCT] Formulated with a single ingredient: 100% pure organic green tea powder with no added sweeteners, colorings, or fillers.",
    "[GENERAL] Culinary-grade matcha is milled from later-harvest tea leaves to yield a bolder, more robustly astringent profile that retains its green tea flavor when paired with milk, sweeteners, or baked goods.",
    "[GENERAL] For lattes and mixed beverages, whisk 1.5 to 2 grams (about 1/2 to 1 teaspoon) of sifted powder with 1 to 2 ounces of water heated between 160°F and 175°F (70°C–80°C) before blending in milk.",
    "[GENERAL] Sifting the powder through a fine-mesh strainer and whisking in a rapid \"W\" or zig-zag motion helps eliminate natural clumps and produces a smooth suspension with uniform microfoam.",
    "[GENERAL] Boiling water should never be poured directly onto matcha powder, as temperatures above 175°F (80°C) scorch the ground leaves and create an overly bitter taste."
